# Unity 2D: Building Your First Indie Game

Unity is the go-to engine for indie developers. This guide covers everything you need to create engaging 2D games.

## Why Unity for Indie Games?

- **Free to Start**: Free until $100K revenue
- **Huge Community**: Tutorials, assets, forums
- **Cross-Platform**: PC, mobile, console, web
- **Asset Store**: Pre-made assets and tools
- **C# Scripting**: Accessible programming language

## Project Setup

### Creating a 2D Project

```
Unity Hub > New Project
├── Template: 2D (Built-in Render Pipeline)
├── Project Name: MyPlatformer
└── Location: Choose folder

Project Structure:
MyPlatformer/
├── Assets/
│   ├── Scripts/
│   ├── Sprites/
│   ├── Prefabs/
│   ├── Scenes/
│   ├── Audio/
│   └── Animations/
├── Packages/
└── ProjectSettings/
```

### Essential 2D Packages

```
Window > Package Manager

Install:
├── 2D Sprite
├── 2D Tilemap
├── 2D Animation
├── 2D Pixel Perfect (for pixel art)
└── Cinemachine (camera system)
```

## Sprite Basics

### Import Settings

```
Select sprite in Project > Inspector:
├── Texture Type: Sprite (2D and UI)
├── Sprite Mode: Single or Multiple
├── Pixels Per Unit: 16 (pixel art) or 100 (HD)
├── Filter Mode: Point (pixel art) or Bilinear
├── Compression: None (for crisp pixels)
└── Pivot: Center or Bottom
```

### Sprite Sheet Slicing

```
Sprite Editor (Inspector > Sprite Editor):
├── Slice Type: Grid by Cell Size
├── Pixel Size: 16x16 (match your art)
├── Pivot: Bottom
└── Apply

Result: Individual sprites for animation
```

## Player Controller

### Basic Movement Script

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class PlayerController : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("Movement")]
    [SerializeField] private float moveSpeed = 8f;
    [SerializeField] private float jumpForce = 16f;

    [Header("Ground Check")]
    [SerializeField] private Transform groundCheck;
    [SerializeField] private LayerMask groundLayer;
    [SerializeField] private float groundCheckRadius = 0.2f;

    private Rigidbody2D rb;
    private Animator animator;
    private SpriteRenderer spriteRenderer;

    private float horizontalInput;
    private bool isGrounded;
    private bool facingRight = true;

    void Start()
    {
        rb = GetComponent<Rigidbody2D>();
        animator = GetComponent<Animator>();
        spriteRenderer = GetComponent<SpriteRenderer>();
    }

    void Update()
    {
        // Input
        horizontalInput = Input.GetAxisRaw("Horizontal");

        // Ground check
        isGrounded = Physics2D.OverlapCircle(
            groundCheck.position, 
            groundCheckRadius, 
            groundLayer
        );

        // Jump
        if (Input.GetButtonDown("Jump") && isGrounded)
        {
            rb.velocity = new Vector2(rb.velocity.x, jumpForce);
        }

        // Flip sprite
        if (horizontalInput > 0 && !facingRight)
            Flip();
        else if (horizontalInput < 0 && facingRight)
            Flip();

        // Update animator
        animator.SetFloat("Speed", Mathf.Abs(horizontalInput));
        animator.SetBool("IsGrounded", isGrounded);
        animator.SetFloat("VerticalVelocity", rb.velocity.y);
    }

    void FixedUpdate()
    {
        // Move
        rb.velocity = new Vector2(horizontalInput * moveSpeed, rb.velocity.y);
    }

    void Flip()
    {
        facingRight = !facingRight;
        spriteRenderer.flipX = !facingRight;
    }

    void OnDrawGizmosSelected()
    {
        if (groundCheck != null)
        {
            Gizmos.color = Color.red;
            Gizmos.DrawWireSphere(groundCheck.position, groundCheckRadius);
        }
    }
}
```

